<main class="home"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> CONTEXT BETWEEN SESAME CONVERSATIONS</div><h1>Pick up where<br><span>you left off.</span></h1><p class="lede">Keep the details, decisions, and open questions you save in Brain ready for your next Sesame call or chat. Same voice. Same connection. Something useful to build on.</p>
<p class="home-boundary">Brain carries forward information saved through its tools. It does not automatically capture every spoken word or import your existing Sesame history.</p>
<div class="continuity-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Save context in one Sesame conversation, retrieve it from Brain in the next conversation using the same connection"><div><span class="diagram-step">01</span><strong>This conversation</strong><small>Save the important detail.</small></div><span class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="diagram-memory"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">b</span><strong>Your saved context</strong><small>Facts · Projects · Open questions</small></div><span class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="diagram-step">02</span><strong>The next conversation</strong><small>Resume with the same voice.</small></div></div>
<section class="connect-card" aria-labelledby="connect-title"><div class="card-top"><h2 id="connect-title">Connect once. Keep going.</h2><span class="small muted">NO DOWNLOAD</span></div><p>In Sesame, open <strong>Agent Hub → Apps</strong> and add an external MCP. Paste this address, sign in, and label the connection. Then ask Sesame to save and resume context through Brain. Additional connections are optional.</p><div class="copy-row"><code id="mcp-address"><%= config.resource %></code><button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy="<%= config.resource %>">Copy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><a class="text-link" href="/docs">Try it across two conversations <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
<div class="principles"><p><strong>Your memory. Your control.</strong> Explore your dashboard, export your record, or clear your memories whenever you like.</p><p><strong>Open source. Vibecoded.</strong> Spec drafted with Claude. Implemented by OpenAI Codex. Human review is recommended before trusting sensitive information.</p></div></main>
